{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_03_data_model_memory", "label": "Memory", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every version is its own row (ADR-0014); kind is declared by the domain adapter and core interprets none; creation (none->VALID) is recorded by the row itself, I2 covers transitions only.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_temporary_fact", "label": "Temporary fact (valid_to)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Temporariness is just an ordinary memory with valid_to filled by the change detector; nothing else marks it (ADR-0015).", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_version_chain", "label": "Version chain (supersedes_id)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Update writes a new row with supersedes_id and retires the old; the chain is supersedes_id only, no supersedes link.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_link", "label": "Link (dependency edge)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stored parent_id -> dependent_id: the dependent is wrong if the parent changes. confidence is linker belief (FR-16 re-check); strength is reliance, unused until idea 6.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_direction_convention", "label": "Link direction convention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assumed by collaborator: stored parent->dependent; prose writes dependent --type--> parent, e.g. eligibility(Acme) --eligibility_of--> cgpa.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_link_classes", "label": "Link classes (core) vs link types (domains)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Core knows two classes with fixed behaviour; each domain link type maps to exactly one; the registry lives in the domain adapter and is applied in the write flow, never in core.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_link_class_depends_on", "label": "Link class: depends_on", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Propagates a change; copied to new version on update; on forget of parent the dependent is hard-deleted (cascade).", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_link_class_snapshot_of", "label": "Link class: snapshot_of", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Does not propagate; not copied to the new version; on forget of parent the link is removed and dependent kept. Makes the correct non-update case for sent applications fall out of the copy rule.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_jobs_link_types", "label": "Link type registry: depends_on_fact, depends_on_time_period, eligibility_of, fit_of, reminder_for, criteria_from, sent_with_resume", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "sent_with_resume is snapshot_of so a new resume never ripples into past applications; all others are depends_on. Provenance to sources is source_ref, not a link, because sources are not memories.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_ripple_semantics", "label": "Ripple semantics (wave by wave, two commits per wave)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trigger is a memory write; engine takes an explicit seed set; wave 1 = dependents along depends_on with no status filter; commit one marks SUSPECT, Resolver decides, commit two appends decisions; only updated/retired seed next wave; keep halts branch; ask parks in PENDING_USER and marks subtree SUSPECT without LLM; stop on empty wave or depth limit with visited set. Engine is a pure iterator and never calls an LLM; sweep resumes events with no completed_at. One transaction per ripple is impossible once a wave waits on a user.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_wave", "label": "Wave (set of dependents resolved together)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each wave is two commits; decisions tagged with wave number; wave 0 = deterministic restoration recorded by an answer.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_seed_set", "label": "Seed set", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Explicit seed set (new version for write, retired memory for expiry/retire) is why copying links to new versions works with no status filter.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_ask_pending_user_parking", "label": "Ask parks memory in PENDING_USER; subtree marked SUSPECT", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assumed; retrieval flags the subtree while user has not answered; \"still holds\" restores deterministically, changed memory starts a new user_answer ripple.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_versioning_link_copy", "label": "Versioning: copy incoming and outgoing depends_on links to the new version", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Incoming links copied so the new version has same dependents (retired dependents not copied; one per dependent,type); outgoing links copied re-pointed at each parent latest version so later parent changes still reach the new version even if the Linker misses; snapshot_of stays on old row; crash rolls back everything (ADR-0014).", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_history_link", "label": "History link", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A link whose parent is superseded; inspector and retrieval graph expansion skip history depends_on links, snapshot_of always shown; the engine applies no such filter.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_changeevent", "label": "ChangeEvent", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One per ripple, created in the trigger write transaction and appended per wave; trigger_kind in ripple|expiry|user_edit|user_answer; completed_at null while open lets the sweep find ripples to resume; makes I2 testable per trigger kind (ADR-0015).", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_forgetevent", "label": "ForgetEvent", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Forget is deletion, not a state change, so it has no ChangeEvent (I7).", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_decision", "label": "Decision record (keep|update|retire|ask)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "memory_id, wave, action, reason, evidence_refs, new_version_id, question (only an ask carries one).", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_validity_states", "label": "Validity states VALID / SUSPECT / RETIRED / PENDING_USER", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Transition table: none->VALID on write; VALID->SUSPECT in wave or below PENDING_USER; SUSPECT->VALID on keep or still-holds; to RETIRED on retire/expiry/new version; any->deleted only via forget API.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_invariant_i1_retrieval_visibility", "label": "Invariant I1: VALID returned, SUSPECT/PENDING_USER flagged, RETIRED never", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retrieval visibility rule.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_invariant_i2_state_changes_recorded", "label": "Invariant I2: every state transition has a ChangeEvent", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Covers transitions between states, not creation; testable per trigger kind.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_invariant_i3_engine_never_calls_llm", "label": "Invariant I3: deterministic scope; engine never calls an LLM", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scope computed by graph traversal only (ADR-0003).", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_invariant_i5_no_unconfirmed_or_invented_facts", "label": "Invariant I5: no unconfirmed or invented facts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Referenced by FR-1 and FR-11.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_invariant_i7_forget", "label": "Invariant I7: forget deletes whole version chain and cascades", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Forget applies to a whole version chain and cascades along depends_on links whose parent is in the chain; ADR-0007 calls this cascading along derived_from links.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_worked_example_cgpa_ripple", "label": "Worked example: cgpa 7.6 -> 7.9 ripple", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "cgpa v2 supersedes v1; incoming links copied; wave 1 = eligibility(Acme) and criteria -> update; wave 2 recommendation; wave 3 empty; Scout re-runs because criteria changed. One ChangeEvent holds all decisions.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_worked_example_temporary_exams", "label": "Worked example: busy-with-exams expiry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fact with valid_to ripples normally; sweep retires it on expiry (trigger_kind=expiry) with the retired fact as seed set; wave 1 = availability restored; no LLM needed to detect expiry.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_03_data_model_worked_example_forget_cgpa", "label": "Worked example: forget my CGPA", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deletes cgpa v1 and v2, the eligibility and criteria memories depending on them and their dependents; writes one ForgetEvent.", "_origin": "semantic"}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_03_data_model", "target": "docs_03_data_model_memory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"source": "docs_03_data_model", "target": "docs_03_data_model_temporary_fact", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"source": "docs_03_data_model", "target": "docs_03_data_model_version_chain", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"source": "docs_03_data_model", "target": "docs_03_data_model_link", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"source": "docs_03_data_model", "target": "docs_03_data_model_direction_convention", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/03-data-model.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0, "_origin"